-- title:
--   Filtered lifts make each coordinate integral
-- statement:
--   Show that every coordinate is integral over the algebra generated by g, given finiteness over the algebra generated by the degree-D weighted components. This is the filtered-lifting step. The statement keeps D positive and the inclusive support bound, including terms of degree below D. Its proof route uses homogeneous power relations and induction on weighted degree to control lower-degree terms when lifting relations. The remaining core is establishing that filtered lift.
-- source:
--   openai/math Ampleness stack: WeightedIdealCurveBound implies eps-ample exceptional twist, hence Serre vanishing and eventual generation of I^n by weight ≤ n(rho+eps) sections.

import Definitions.Def_OAI_PiExponent_WeightedIdealCurveCriterion
